{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Segoe UI;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green102\blue204;\red0\green130\blue70;\red196\green89\blue17;\red178\green34\blue34;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\f0\fs28 Image Converter \endash  quick guide\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\cf3 What it is for\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa100\fi-360\li720\bullet\tab Batch-convert images in a folder among \cf2 JPEG, PNG, BMP, GIF, WEBP, ICO, SVG, and PDF\cf0 .\par
\bullet\tab \cf2 Preview thumbnails\cf0 , pick files, and convert without a separate export step.\par
\bullet\tab Useful for preparing web assets, icons, PDF snapshots, and format cleanup on Windows.\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\cf3 Getting started\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa100\fi-360\li720 1.\tab Choose an image folder (\cf1 File \endash  Open folder\cf0 , or \cf1 Browse\cf0  on the main window).\par
2.\tab \cf2 Thumbnails\cf0  load in the review list. Drag a folder or files onto the list to set the folder.\par
3.\tab \cf1 Select\cf0  one or more images.\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\cf3 Converting\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa100\fi-360\li720\bullet\tab \cf1 Right-click\cf0  a selected thumbnail \endash  \cf1 Convert to\cf0  \endash  pick a format.\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Resize\cf0  \endash  \cf2 0.5x, 0.75x, 2x, or 4x\cf0  saves a new file beside the original: same name with \cf2 _scaled\cf0  before the extension (e.g. \cf2 photo_scaled.png\cf0 ). \cf2 JPEG, PNG, BMP, GIF, WEBP, and ICO\cf0  only.\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Convert to Icon\cf0  creates or rebuilds \cf2 .ico\cf0  files using the \cf2 ICO size\cf0  and \cf2 background\cf0  settings at the top (white, black, or transparent letterbox).\par
\bullet\tab Set \cf2 Background\cf0  to \cf2 Transparent (preserve alpha)\cf0  for \cf2 PNG, GIF, WEBP, ICO, or SVG\cf0 . Keeps existing alpha; keys out a uniform edge color on flat backgrounds. \cf4 Not AI removal\cf0  for complex photos (\cf4 JPG and BMP do not support transparency\cf0 ).\par
\bullet\tab New files are saved in the \cf3 same folder\cf0  (same name, new extension) and selected after convert.\par
\bullet\tab \cf3 If a file already exists\cf0 , you are asked to \cf1 confirm overwrite\cf0 .\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\cf4 SVG output (important)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa100\fi-360\li720\bullet\tab \cf1 Convert to SVG\cf0  does \b\cf4 not\b0\cf0  vector-trace your image (no paths or shapes are created).\par
\bullet\tab The app saves the picture as \cf2 PNG\cf0  data inside a standard \cf2 .svg\cf0  file (an embedded image tag with base64 data).\par
\bullet\tab The file opens as SVG everywhere, but it is still a \cf4 bitmap\cf0 : zooming in will show \cf4 pixels\cf0 , and vector editors will not give you editable outlines from it.\par
\bullet\tab Use this when you need a \cf2 .svg\cf0  file for a tool or workflow; use \cf2 PNG\cf0  or \cf2 WEBP\cf0  for normal photos; use a vector tracer (e.g. Inkscape) if you need real scalable paths.\par
\bullet\tab If the source is already a vector \cf2 .svg\cf0 , it is rasterized first, then wrapped again \endash  \cf4 original paths are not kept\cf0 .\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\cf3 Other actions\b0\cf0  (\cf1 right-click\cf0  or \cf1 File\cf0  menu)\par
\pard\sa100\fi-360\li720\bullet\tab \cf1 File\cf0  menu groups: choose folder and refresh; open image or application folder in Explorer; paste and undo; exit.\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Copy\cf0  / \cf1 Copy image path\cf0\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Rename\cf0  (\cf1 F2\cf0 )\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Delete\cf0\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Open file location\cf0\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Open by Paint\cf0  or \cf1 Paint.NET\cf0\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Paste image\cf0  from clipboard into the folder\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\cf3 Keyboard shortcuts\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa100\fi-360\li720\bullet\tab \cf1 F5\cf0  \endash  refresh review\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 F2\cf0  \endash  rename selected file\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Ctrl+C\cf0  \endash  copy path (when list is focused)\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Ctrl+V\cf0  / \cf1 Ctrl+P\cf0  \endash  paste image\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Ctrl+Z\cf0  \endash  undo last operation\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Delete\cf0  \endash  delete selected files\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\cf3 Tips\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa100\fi-360\li720\bullet\tab Use \cf2 small / medium / large\cf0  thumbnail size to fit more or fewer items on screen.\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Undo\cf0  removes converted output files from the last successful batch.\par
\bullet\tab \cf1 Cancel\cf0  stops a conversion batch in progress.\par
\pard\sa100\sl276\slmult1\cf3\fs20 Color key:\cf0\fs22  \cf1 blue = actions and shortcuts\cf0 ; \cf2 green = formats and features\cf0 ; \cf3 orange = important notes\cf0 ; \cf4 red = limitations and warnings\cf0 .\par
